# storybook-annotakit — optional environment knobs (template; all read ONCE at boot)
#
# Copy to `.env` next to the Storybook project root, then RESTART `storybook
# dev`. ⚠ .env holds a SECRET: add `.env` to .gitignore BEFORE writing the
# token (the engine never commits it, but a bare `git add -A` would).
#
# Everything below is optional — with none of these set, the addon runs in
# fully-working LOCAL mode (threads, digests, resolve, REST API; no GitHub).
# The GitHub mirror switches on when BOTH a token and a repo resolve.

# --- GitHub mirror ---------------------------------------------------------

# ANNOTAKIT_GH_TOKEN=ghp_xxx            # PAT (classic, `repo` scope on one feedback repo is enough)
# ANNOTAKIT_GH_REPO=owner/name          # issue-landing repo (may differ from the code repo; else
#                                       #   git-remote / package.json autodetect — which FAILS
#                                       #   SILENTLY in non-git projects, so pin it)
# ANNOTAKIT_GH_LABELS=annotakit,workstream:payments
#                                       # ALL labels applied to created issues; the pull listing
#                                       #   filters by them (AND) — the multi-workstream knob
# ANNOTAKIT_GH_AUTO=0                   # 0|false|off|no = mirror off → local mode (default: on)
# ANNOTAKIT_GH_POLL=60                  # pull interval in SECONDS (default 60; 0 = pull on POST /sync only)
# ANNOTAKIT_GH_INTERVAL=700             # mirror worker tick in ms (default 700)
# ANNOTAKIT_GH_API=https://api.github.com
#                                       # custom API base (GitHub Enterprise / test fake)

# --- API access ------------------------------------------------------------

# ANNOTAKIT_API_KEY=                    # opt-in shared secret. Loopback (localhost) peers ALWAYS
#                                       #   pass — the key only gates NON-loopback clients, which
#                                       #   must send it as the `x-annotakit-key` header (401
#                                       #   without it; with no key configured at all,
#                                       #   non-loopback gets 403). Only needed when something
#                                       #   outside your machine must reach the API.

# --- advanced --------------------------------------------------------------

# ANNOTAKIT_ENV_TRACKED_OK=1            # silence the "token in a TRACKED .env" boot warning —
#                                       #   deliberate "git is the disk" sandbox setups only
